<BaseLayout title="Resources & sources" description="Starting points for primary and specialist information on UXO and explosive remnants of war.">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Source library</p><h1>Start with the source.</h1><p class="lead">This is a small, growing set of authoritative starting points—not a substitute for local advice, technical assessment, or specialist clearance guidance.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container split"><div><p class="eyebrow">Standards &amp; law</p><h2>Use the primary framework.</h2></div><div class="copy"><ul class="source-list"><li><strong><a href="https://www.mineactionstandards.org/standards/07-11/">IMAS 07.11: Land release</a></strong><p>The reference for land-release process, all reasonable effort, residual contamination, and residual risk.</p></li><li><strong><a href="https://www.mineactionstandards.org/standards/04-10/">IMAS 04.10: Glossary of mine-action terms</a></strong><p>Authoritative definitions for UXO, AXO, ERW, EO, and related terms.</p></li><li><strong><a href="https://ihl-databases.icrc.org/en/ihl-treaties/ccw-protocol-v/technical-annex">CCW Protocol V technical annex</a></strong><p>International framework covering recording, warnings, risk education, marking, fencing, monitoring, and clearance.</p></li></ul></div></div></section>
<section class="section section--deep"><div class="container split"><div><p class="eyebrow">Humanitarian mine action</p><h2>Data and operational context.</h2></div><div class="copy"><ul class="source-list"><li><strong><a href="https://www.unmas.org/en">United Nations Mine Action Service</a></strong><p>United Nations mine-action information, country programmes, and risk-reduction work.</p></li><li><strong><a href="https://www.icrc.org/en/what-we-do/weapon-contamination">ICRC: Weapon contamination</a></strong><p>Explosive contamination, civilian impacts, and the humanitarian response.</p></li><li><strong><a href="https://the-monitor.org/en-gb/reports/2025/landmine-monitor-2025.aspx">Landmine Monitor</a></strong><p>Annual, cited reporting on mines, cluster munitions, and explosive remnants of war. Read the category and year before reusing any number.</p></li><li><strong><a href="https://www.mineactionreview.org/">Mine Action Review</a></strong><p>Independent research on mine-action progress, including country-by-country clearance reporting.</p></li></ul></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container split"><div><p class="eyebrow">Environment &amp; water</p><h2>The hazard can outlast the explosion.</h2></div><div class="copy"><ul class="source-list"><li><strong><a href="https://www.epa.gov/fedfac/military-munitions-response-program">U.S. EPA: Military Munitions Response Program</a></strong><p>Background on munitions and explosives of concern, and potential explosive-residue and metal contamination at former military sites.</p></li><li><strong><a href="https://coast.noaa.gov/digitalcoast/tools/mec.html">NOAA: Munitions and Explosives of Concern</a></strong><p>U.S. outer-continental-shelf mapping and data context; historic offshore locations are often incomplete or uncertain.</p></li><li><strong><a href="https://www.ospar.org/work-areas/rsc/munitions">OSPAR: Munitions</a></strong><p>Northeast Atlantic work on dumped conventional and chemical munitions and reported encounters.</p></li><li><strong><a href="https://helcom.fi/publications/thematic-assessment-on-hazardous-submerged-objects-in-the-baltic-sea-volume-1-warfare-materials-in-the-baltic-sea/">HELCOM: Warfare materials in the Baltic Sea</a></strong><p>2025 thematic assessment of hazardous submerged warfare materials, with a focus on conventional munitions.</p></li></ul></div></div></section>
<section class="section section--quiet"><div class="container split"><div><p class="eyebrow">Watch &amp; learn</p><h2>UXO.INFO video resources.</h2></div><div class="copy"><ul class="source-list"><li><strong><a href="https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLOmbSc4tcfSY">UXO.INFO YouTube playlist</a></strong><p>A growing collection of UXO.INFO video resources. YouTube opens in a separate service and may apply its own data practices.</p></li></ul></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
